module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a call expression is erased by v2 normalize before resolve runs, so every reference it carries -- callee and arguments -- is invisible to name resolution and the refusal a missing declaration should raise has nothing to fire on** (INVALID STATE: v2.compiler.normalize, via v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold, lowers a function body that is a call into a Transform node whose only child is the `dag_token_lbrace` atom. The callee identity and every argument subtree are dropped. The module then passes normalize and resolve Accepted, with no diagnostic of any severity).",

    "HARM. v2 name resolution fails OPEN for the whole call-expression population, declared and undeclared alike. A call to a name no declaration provides is Accepted. The namespace cut's census rests on a delete-first premise, that removing an authority makes every real dependent REFUSE LOUDLY, and that premise is void for every dependent reached through a call. For the observed call shapes, erasure prevents the missing-callee resolution refusal from firing. Consequently a refusal roster cannot establish completeness of affected call dependents from absence of refusals. The affected population has not been established by these receipts. Native census mode separately performs no resolution and therefore cannot establish binding-refusal completeness. A native run with no passing call-bearing identities does not by itself identify lowering as the cause of every refused identity.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, because two neighbouring rows look like this one and are not. `unresolved_callee_conflated_with_dispatched_elsewhere` is the v1 ExprCall-tail class: there the callee reaches the classifier and the miss is absorbed later. Here the callee never reaches resolve at all. And the earlier dated measurements (v2.test.claim.staged_front_end unbound_symbol_reason_note, v2.test.claim.dag_acceptance frontier_arm_note) attributed the silence to resolve. That was the wrong stage: resolve is correct over the tree it receives, and the tree has already lost the call. A wall authored in resolve would therefore be a decoration (DESIGN section 4b), because the undeclared-callee RED and the declared-callee positive control arrive as identical trees.",

    "RECEIPT (2026-09-12, still-eagle-447, NAMESPACE XL-2 scoping). The normalized tree was dumped for five bodies via prepare_grammar, parse_module_prepared and normalize -- the calls v2.compiler.program_assembly program_assembly_read_to_normalized_root_prepared makes, and so the census route's own hand-off (v2.compiler.compile native_test_context_from_ingest). `{ k }` keeps `Atom:k`. `{ x }` over a parameter keeps `Atom:x`. `{ g(x: 1) }` with g declared, `{ zzz(x: 1) }` and `{ zzz(1) }` with zzz undeclared all become `Transform [ Atom:dag_token_lbrace ]`. The unprepared parse_module route (v2.compiler.staged_front_end run_front_end) dumps identically, so this is not a second lossy route beside a faithful one.",

    "EVIDENCE LEVEL, stated so the receipt is not read one rung high. The dumps ran the v2 .dag through the gunbc interpreter at main f9d37e43a1, and a structural node-count fold (not a printer) agrees: the parse tree grows with a call's arguments and nesting, while the normalized body of { g(x: 1) } is exactly one node larger than { k } -- the Transform and its lbrace atom -- and { g(x: h(y: 5)) } is no larger than that. A second named argument adds one node, so the lowering keeps something per extra argument, but none of the callee or argument content. That the natively emitted normalize behaves identically is not executed. The native route gives no contrary evidence: its receipt on the #10940 head (eager-raven-113, 2026-09-12) holds exactly one Passed identity, a literal-bodied smoke test, and every richer body refuses before or at eval (v2.compiler.infer node_grounding_frontier_note). So no route has been observed to lower a call faithfully.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder -- silent wrongness. The compiler Accepts a program with an undeclared callee and reports nothing.",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether a name is bound in the containment index is decidable, and v2 resolve already refuses an unbound VALUE name with `resolve_reason_unbound_symbol`. The missing piece is not an authority but the lowering preserving what resolve needs.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability: v2 body lowering PRESERVES every call expression's callee and argument subtrees into the normalized tree on every v2 route that feeds resolve, so that resolve receives the callee as a reference. The climb's evidence is executed, and resolution alone does not discharge it. The repair that fires this trigger must show, by execution: (i) a call with a DECLARED callee executes through the native route and returns the expected ARGUMENT-DEPENDENT result, so that the argument subtree is demonstrably carried and consumed rather than merely present; (ii) a call with an UNDECLARED callee refuses at RESOLVE with a typed, located missing-binding cause -- at resolve, not later at grounding, emission or eval, since a refusal arriving downstream is consistent with the callee never having reached resolve at all; (iii) controls that discriminate ARGUMENT-subtree loss specifically, over the additional-argument and nested-call shapes named above, such that restoring the erasure makes those regression assertions FAIL rather than leaving them green. An invalid specimen that is Accepted is a FAILING must-refuse assertion, not evidence of anything. The prepared and unprepared routes and the native realization are distinct evidence paths and one passing route does not stand in for the others. A resolve-side check, a census count, or a migration of known call sites does not fire this trigger, because none of them makes the call reach resolve. These are requirements on the repair's evidence, not executions owed before this row lands.",

    "CENSUS CONSEQUENCE, recorded because the cut consumes it: the whole-tree native census (the emitted closure binary's census mode) runs only tokenize, parse and normalize per file and never calls resolve, so its roster carries front-end refusals only. Restoring call lowering does not by itself add resolve refusals to that census. That needs the census mode to resolve per module as well.",

    "CONSUMER-SIDE RECEIPT AND A SECOND SHAPE, 2026-09-13 (deep-newt-301, dispatched on `fold_shape_visible_to_no_lens`). The same route (tokenize, parse_module, normalize) was dumped for fold-family calls, which this class also erases, and for a body that is a `let` followed by a call. `{ fold(xs, init: 0, f: step) }` and `{ g(xs, init: 0, f: step) }` both become `Transform [ Atom dag_token_lbrace, Atom dag_token_int_literal, Atom step ]`: the named-argument VALUES survive as positional operands with their labels and the callee and positional `xs` dropped, which refines the earlier receipt's `a second named argument adds one node` -- what is kept is the value atom of each named argument, not the argument. The let form is a DIFFERENT erasure shape under the same class: `{ let seed = 0 \n fold(xs, init: seed, f: fn(acc, x) { .. }) }` lowers to a Bind whose body is a bare left/right sequence spine with `fold` as its leftmost atom and every right projection an empty Conj -- here the callee SURVIVES and the arguments, including an fn literal, do not, with the production shells stripped. So the two shapes lose complementary halves and neither carries a call. THE CONSUMER THIS SILENCES beyond resolve: `v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.analyze`, a required root lens at the compile door, enumerates fold sites by seam Loop or by surface fold call, and both are produced only where fold_lowering runs BEFORE this erasure -- the sole-body position. A planted quadratic after a let, in a match arm or in an if branch is Accepted with no finding, in every step spelling; enrolled RED at `gunbc.explicit_witness_admission` as `let_prefixed_fold_copy_is_caught`, `match_arm_fold_copy_is_caught` and `declared_named_step_fold_copy_is_caught` in `src/v2/test/claim/long/accumulator_copy_fold_analysis_test.dag`, each dissolving on this row's trigger. The trigger's clause (iii) gains a shape: the controls must cover the let-prefixed body, whose loss is the argument half rather than the callee half.",

    "PARTIAL REPAIR OF ONE SHAPE, AND THE TRIGGER IS NOT FIRED BY IT (2026-09-19, gunbc#11612). A call whose CALLEE is a dotted chain -- `wall.peer.peer_leaf()` -- previously lowered to the chain's FIRST ATOM with the remaining segments and the call itself dropped, so it lost both halves at once. v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_dotted_call_optional now reads that shape off the same walk as body_lower_dotted_reference_optional and lowers it to a Transform whose operator is the qualified-name spine, consulted in the one arm where body_lower_try_postfix_projection would otherwise refuse a continuing chain; the receiver-method shape `r.method(x)` keeps its existing arm untouched. Executed evidence: v2.test.claim.body_lowering_qualified_path body_lowering_qualified_call_reaches_arrow_body runs tokenize, parse and normalize over the real productions and reads the real arrow body, asserting the Transform's first positional child is the three-segment spine, with the bare local body `peer_leaf` as the positive control in the same claim. WHAT THIS DOES NOT DISCHARGE, stated so the row is not read one rung high: this row's trigger names the whole call-expression population and demands argument-dependent NATIVE execution, a resolve-stage refusal for an undeclared callee, and controls that discriminate ARGUMENT-subtree loss. None of those is delivered here, the argument subtrees of other call shapes are untouched, and the row stays open at its stated rung.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
